<p>I ran across a photo in my library from years ago showing my computer running AIM. A wave of nostalgia washed over me, as you can imagine.</p>
<!-- more -->
<p>Then, yesterday I read Veronica's post, <a href="https://veronicaexplains.net/open-oscar-server/">Here's how I host my own AIM server</a> and I had to try it.</p>
<p>Read that post for all the details you'd need, but basically all I did was...</p>
<ol>
<li>Run the server binary on a VPS with the IP configured as a listener</li>
<li>Installed AIM 5.1 via the <a href="https://archive.org/details/aim513036">AIM installer from archive.org</a> using <a href="https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/wikis/Download">wine</a> (on Linux)</li>
<li>Changed the AIM config to use my server IP.</li>
</ol>
<p>That was pretty much it.</p>
